# Async checkpoint pipeline

When the job is multi-step or needs parallel workers, open `~/.cursor/skills/async-checkpoint-pipeline/SKILL.md`. Skip for a short in-scope parent answer.

## Model by role

Newest listed slug for family and tier; state it. If the preferred tier is missing, use the newest family slug on the allowlist and name the gap. MUST NOT hardcode unlisted versions. MUST NOT use `*-fast` or GPT Luna for Architect, Bind, Diagnose, Deploy, Visual, or Web. Cursor Task `inherit` is forbidden on a role-tagged atom.

- Architect = Opus thinking -- thin root plan or complex diagnosis only
- Bind = Grok high -- plan and atom cards
- Diagnose = Grok high -- cause and proof
- Implement = Gemini flash high -- one atom
- Deploy = Grok high -- ship, verify, rollback
- Web = Gemini flash -- live docs
- Visual = Kimi high -- visual review
- Prose = Gemini flash -- prose
- Unclear = Grok high -- uncertain route

## Spawn (one-liners)

After Bind-ready atom cards: one background `Task` per ready disjoint atom in the same message (`subagent_type=generalPurpose`, `model=<slug>`, `run_in_background=true`). Then end the turn. Checkpoint is the next parent turn. Grok parent does Bind on parent; still emit cards before Implement.

Multitask Mode governs spawn-async and end-turn only. Shared MemNet session: `memnet-multitask`. Both faces visible: `sysmledge-cursor-multitask`.
